Following a security audit, the xFusionCorp Industries security team has opted to enhance application and server security with SELinux. 
To initiate testing, the following requirements have been established for App server 1 in the Stratos Datacenter:

Install the required SELinux packages.

Permanently disable SELinux for the time being; it will be re-enabled after necessary configuration changes.

No need to reboot the server, as a scheduled maintenance reboot is already planned for tonight.

Disregard the current status of SELinux via the command line; the final status after the reboot should be disabled.

SOLUTION
To meet the requirement of permanently disabling SELinux on App Server 1 without rebooting immediately, you need to install the relevant packages and modify the configuration file. The core operation is to edit /etc/selinux/config and change the SELinux status to disabled.

🛠️ Operation Steps
Log in to App Server 1 and switch to the root user.

Install SELinux-related packages (for RHEL/CentOS systems):

bash
yum install -y selinux-policy selinux-policy-targeted policycoreutils
This ensures the required policy and tool packages are present on the system, facilitating future re-enabling .

Edit the configuration file to disable permanently:

bash
vi /etc/selinux/config
Find the line SELINUX=enforcing and change it to:

text
SELINUX=disabled
Save and exit .

Verify the configuration:

bash
grep ^SELINUX= /etc/selinux/config
The expected output should be SELINUX=disabled .

💡 Key Reminders
No need to reboot: As per the requirement, do not reboot the server now. This configuration will only take effect after the scheduled reboot tonight, and getenforce may still display Enforcing currently, which is normal .

Final status: After the reboot, the system will not load the SELinux policy, and the final status will be disabled .

To help you verify the results after the reboot
After tonight's scheduled reboot, you can run getenforce to confirm whether the output is Disabled. If you need further confirmation or encounter any issues, feel free to let me know.
